exports[`golden sections > mystmd-guide #style-sheet 1`] = `
"(style-sheet)=
## Add a Style Sheet ({abbr}\`CSS (Cascading Style Sheet)\`) to your website

The [default MyST website themes](#default-web-themes) support bundling a custom [style-sheet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS). This can be used to introduce custom {abbr}\`CSS (Cascading Style Sheet)\` styling to your website. To include a custom {abbr}\`CSS (Cascading Style Sheet)\` file as part of your website build, you can define the [**style** (*file*)](#template-site-myst-book-theme-style) option, e.g.

\`\`\`{code-block} yaml
:emphasize-lines: 3
:linenos:

site:
  options:
    style: ./my-style.css
\`\`\`

\`\`\`{embed}
\`\`\`

For example, the style-sheet could contain styling for \`em\` elements nested below a particular \`text-gradient\` class:

\`\`\`{include} public/style.css
\`\`\`"
`;
